## §1.3 THE RENDERED SLOT BINDS THE CLAUSE AROUND IT · binds ALL

| id | the claim that would be false | the field / file:line that denies it | binds | folded |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| **F1-117** | a clause NEGATING or arguing against what a `proper` fill's own words assert | `{seat}` can render `'Corrupt Council'`, `'Corrupt City Council'`, `'Shadow Senate'` (`rulingStructure.js:245-256`, `:264-283`, `:443-452`); `{counterpart}` can render `'Military/Guard'`, `'War Council'`, `'Conversion Enforcement Office'` (`stressFactions.js:105-107`). "Nothing criminal has reached the Corrupt Council of X" contradicts itself AT RENDER TIME on every town that fills it that way | ALL | NF-1, D-F27, RT2.1-24, RT2.4-19, PS-01, PS-02, OV-19, W21c |
| **F1-118** | reading a class word INSIDE a rendered NAME as a body or a standing | `rulingStructure.js:596`; `stressFactions.js:105-107`; `OV-18` — a `proper` slot carries neither class nor visibility | ALL | OV-18, rule 3 |
| **F1-119** | naming `{seat}` and `{faction}` as TWO actors in one unit | `powerStateProse.js:860`, `:875-876`, `:900-901`, `:909`, `:953`, `:962` — both fill from ONE `governingName` string, so one actor outweighs itself. ⚠ also §1.6 W-05 (DS-POW-6 fills the "captured house" with the governing body) | POW | PS-03, P-R2, P-R3, P-R5d, RT2.4-20 |
| **F1-120** | attributing a TREATY's terms, signature or intent to `{counterpart}` | `warFaithStateProse.js:690-694`, `:795`, `:930-933` — the fill is `war.occupation.occupierName \|\| war.counterpart`, the occupier or the lone siege party, NEVER the document's side (`treatyDocument.js:359-361`). Side-neutral cells and `{term}` are the safe forms | WF POW | W25b, PS-11, WF-35, RT2.6R-04, OV-29 |
| **F1-121** | "the garrison" bare, for the OCCUPIER's force | the occupation record is `{occupierId, state, resistance}` with NO garrison field (`occupationStatus.js:74-103`); `hasGarrison` is the town's OWN roster row. **Costs one possessive**: "the occupier's men", "the men who hold the gate now" | WF STR DEF | W25a, RT2.1-42, S-F7, W-24 |
| **F1-122** | binding `occupierHoldings.*` to THIS town's arms | `holderTable.js:199`, `:599-615` — the holder resolves on the settlement passed, so the OCCUPIED town's militia is cited for the OCCUPIER's overextension; the slot roles are inverted against the reader that shares their name (`warFaithStateProse.js:282-294`) | WF | W-27, W-35, RT2.6-40, WF-36, RT2.6R-12 |
| **F1-123** | naming the OCCUPIER as one thing | `occupationStatus.js:83-96` spells it as a foreign TOWN's name; `warStatus.js:318-335` and `pulseKernel.js:1150` spell it as the OCCUPIED town's installed `governingName` or the literal `'occupation authority'`. **Say which** | WF | RT2.6-15, OV-29, NF-6 |
| **F1-124** | "the muster" with no possessor on the treaty block | `treatyDocument.js:58` ("the compelled banner still answers the muster" — the COUNTERPART's call) against `:63` ("no muster gathers where none is allowed" — the TOWN's arms). ⚠ ENGINE self-contradiction: seat the possessor | WF | RT2.6-03, W-25, OV-34 |
| **F1-125** | "the seat" or "the patron" with no possessor on the warFaith block | `treatyDocument.js:72-76` (the treaty-installed seat) vs `religionState.js:620` (the faith standing); `brokeragePatronage.js:60` vs `religionState.js:620`. Two records, one word, both shippable on one dossier | WF | RT2.6-14, RT2.6-28, W-23, OV-13 |
| **F1-126** | **a minted PROPER NAME borne by the face rather than a slot** — a person, a tavern, a lane, a family | a pooled face is authored ONCE and drawn by every town whose key matches, so the name prints identically across a region. No per-town field denies it, which is why no licence test ever caught it. The town's own NPC roster and the `{npc}` slots are the name authority | ALL | NF-4, W27b |

## §1.4 THE FROZEN/LIVE SEAM — read this before charging any floor-1 finding

The defense tab is **two clocks**. `generateDefenseProfile` has exactly ONE caller (`steps/assembleSettlement.js`), so `defenseProfile.{scores, readiness, institutions, economicGates}`, `economicState.safetyProfile.*` and `economicState.compound.inst` are **generation-time snapshots never rebuilt**; every ruin path stamps the roster row immutably (`calamityKernel.js:251`, `settlementLifecycleFirstClass.js:601`, `magicRegimeLifecycle.js:355`) and the snapshot holds the pre-ruin objects by reference (`defenseInstitutionBuckets.js:35-50`). The desks were cured to read `standingDefenseForces` / `liveInstitutions`; **the surfaces beside them were not.**

| id | the collision | which side is the record | disposition |
|---|---|---|---|
| **W-01** | `hasMercenary: true` (`priorityHelpers.js:49-51`) against `forces.mercenary.present: false` (`defenseInstitutionBuckets.js:98-100`) on a Hireling-hall town | neither — two engine surfaces | **WIRING** (CAR 8b-W-2). No sentence satisfies both; no face may be charged on this town |
| **W-02** | a `Household levy` on the roster (`institutionalCatalog.js:104`) against `NO organized force at all` (`defenseStateProse.js:1273-1274`) | neither | **WIRING.** But the pool's OWN key consults six buckets, so a face naming any of the six on that key IS a finding (`defenseStateProse.js:1273`) |
| **W-03** | a custom "Night Watch": invisible to the buckets (`nativeSemanticName` returns `''`, `customContentSemanticAuthority.js:40-48`), visible to `SECURITY_INSTITUTION_RE` (`corruption.js:665-666`) | the ROSTER | **WIRING + F1-30.** Never assert the absence |
| **W-04** | DS-GEN-17 `GARRISONED`'s gloss ("a force the town PAYS for") against its key, satisfied by `walls` · `citadel` · a `Watchtower` alone (`priorityHelpers.js:45`) | the KEY | **F1-04/F1-02 finding** on a pay claim; the gloss is a **WIRING** row |
| **W-05** | DS-POW-6's `{faction}` documented as the CAPTURED HOUSE, filled with the GOVERNING body (`powerStateProse.js:900-901`, `:962`) | the FILL | **WIRING.** The accusation lands on the wrong power by the fill, not the writer |
| **W-06** | three PLAYER `mobilization:` pools carded `audience: DM only` (`wiringCensus.js:1681`; `warFaithStateProse.js:251-262`) | the LEAF | **WIRING** |
| **W-07** | a granary READING printed with no granary row — capacity falls through to 1.5/2.0 months (`foodStockpile.js:190-193`) | the ROSTER | **WIRING;** F1-09 still governs the building |
| **W-08** | `Town watch`'s `Gate duty: {on: true}` (`institutionServices.js:1324`) against `safetyProfile.js:463-464`'s "no gates to bribe" | neither | **WIRING.** Follow the services panel; a writer agreeing with either surface cannot be failed |
| **W-09** | `threatAssessment.js:59`, `:66`, `:80` hardcode "Palisade and citizen militia" and "watch rotations" on branches firing for ANY walls row, including `Town walls` and `Massive walls` | the ROSTER | **WIRING (owner, OW-20).** ⚠ this directly undercuts F1-32: the rewrite may be correct about stone while the row beside it says palisade |
| **W-10** | four of DS-DEF-2's five pools are keyed on BOOLEANS and judged beside a continuous `scoreBand(scores.military)` badge (`defenseStateProse.js:454-595` vs `DefenseTab.jsx:322-341`) | both — different inputs | **INSTRUMENT.** See §S-1: the card must print the band spread over the key's domain before any intensity word is refutable |
| **W-11** | DS-DEF-2's box is two clocks inside one `<div>`: rows 1–2 live, rows 3–5 snapshot (`DefenseTab.jsx:317-321`) | the LIVE rows | **WIRING** |
| **W-12** | `safetyLabel` (first-survey, zero pulse writers) against the live `defense_readiness` band on SubstrateTab (`SubstrateTab.jsx:33-52`) | neither — two measurements | **RULED at §R-2: not a contradiction** |
| **W-13** | DS-DEF-5's and DS-DEF-11's block TITLES name `defenseProfile.institutions` / `defenseProfileHasWalls`; both read `standingDefenseForces` | the CENSUS | **INSTRUMENT.** Fix the titles before the marker re-runs; they poison every skeleton |
| **W-14** | a covert-economy sentence player-audible: DS-ECO-6's two canonical rows are FROZEN literals with no `dm-only` mark inside a block declared wholly dm-only (`economy.generated.js:1595`; `EconomicsTab.jsx:664`) | the ANNEX | **WIRING** |
| **W-15** | `'Unknown Faction (hidden)'` reaching a player face through `{counterpart}` (`stressFactions.js:105-107`; `properFill` does not reject it) | the FIELD | **WIRING** |
| **W-16** | `causalReceipt` invents "for it comes scarce this season" to the reader (`marketPrices.js:213-218`) | — | **WIRING** — a floor-2 breach in the PRODUCT. Never lift the clause verbatim (craft) |
| **W-17** | DS-STR-2's anaphora binds to the DS-STR-1 banner above it — a DIFFERENT record class chosen by `.find()` (`stressorsStateProse.js:355-359`) | the BANNER | **F1 finding, PAGE grain.** Name the crisis. No pool-grain refuter can see it |
| **W-18** | `rollStressSummary` = `{profit: rng() < 0.45}` (`stressNarrative.js:42`) — 45 % of wartime towns assert a reinforced garrison above the corpus face | — | **UNCHECKABLE by any list.** Needs the render: §S-2 |
| **W-19** | `deriveDefenseGroupLabel` mints "The watch" on a `Watchtower` — a masonry tower (`governanceNarrative.js:499-506`; `institutionServices.js:1561`) | the ROSTER | **WIRING** |

**⛔ THE TIE-BREAK (§R-1, the chair's ruling — read it before you write a finding).** A floor-1 finding carries THREE fields: the face, the denying surface, and **which side is the record**. The record is a FIELD, a FLAG, a BAND, a LABEL or a ROSTER ROW. Where the denying surface is engine PROSE or a stale snapshot, **the face stands** and you file a WIRING row instead. In four of the five sharpest measured collisions the corpus face is the truthful party; a floor that charges the truthful party would force the rewrite to re-introduce ruin-blindness in order to agree with a defect.

---

# FLOOR 2 — THE PROMISE `[F2]`

*A seed is a STARTING world forever. Atmosphere is free; a countable, datable or elapsed fact is not. **These rows are decidable from the face's grammar alone** — you need no world model to see a count word, a perfect tense or a frequency adverb.*

| id | the claim that would be false | why | binds |
|---|---|---|---|
| **F2-01** | **ANY magnitude the read does not hand you**, in a digit OR in a word: a count, a share, a sum, a price, a volume, a distance, a headcount, a death toll, an attendance, a congregation, a garrison's size. "Forty on the roll", "a handful", "no more than a dozen", "three hundred devout" | the engine's band vocabularies are CLOSED (`shareBandLabel`, `scoreBand`, `AGE_BANDS`, `treatyAgeBandWord`, `bandedStock`, `QUANTITY_BANDS`). `demographicsHerald.js:70-80` shows the trap: 41 souls reads "a hundred or so". **A magnitude the read does not carry is not spoken at all.** "More of them than the town can feed" is the hook | ALL |
| **F2-02** | **ANY date, year, season, month or duration** — "three winters ago", "since midsummer", "for six generations", "three months' arrears", "how long the patron has held the seat" | `history.age` is frozen at birth, user-settable (`ConfigurationPanel.jsx:419-431`) and rerollable; `tenure` is NEVER projected (`religionState.js:620`); every birth condition sits at `elapsedTicks: 0` (`activeConditions.js:879-902`) | ALL |
| **F2-03** | **A FOUNDING, a raising, a building, a first — narrated** | "newly founded", "built in the old lord's time", "raised three winters ago". `institutionFounding.js` is the engine's own precedent: *"ABSENCE IS THE TYPED VALUE… no arm ever invents a year"* — the closed kinds are `FOUNDED` / `FOUNDED_UNDATED` / `PRE_SEED` | ALL |
| **F2-04** | **AN EVENT THE RECORD DID NOT RUN** — "the healer left", "the mill burned", "the route was cut", "the transfer happened", "the seat was lost" | `previousGovernments` is empty on 48 of 48 generated towns (`rulingPower.js:400-404`); a service absence records no departure; a fall token records no contest | ALL |
| **F2-05** | **AN ELAPSED COURSE** — the perfect, the durative, the comparative-against-a-past, the ordinal over events, the modal future. "has stood", "still", "no longer", "as ever", "since", "thinner than it was", "again", "the second time", "will hold", "would not last a winter" | `ageBands.js` is the constitution's own PIN: `HISTORICIZE_BAND = 'years-past'` — *"historicizing language ('the lean years') is impossible below the YEARS threshold."* A birth-time STATE carries no origin stamp at all, so it can bear no temporal register whatever. And the pulse ADJUDICATES every prediction (`calamityKernel`, `foodStockpile`, `warCosts`) | ALL |
| **F2-06** | **A RATE** — "more often than not", "most nights", "seldom closed", "three times a week", "every spring" | nothing bands a rate anywhere in the engine. ⛔ **The chair's own ADDENDUM 14 example is withdrawn in its rate form.** "The gate stands open" is lawful; "the gate stands open more often than not" is not. See §S-3 for the ruling and its limits | ALL |
| **F2-07** | **AN AGE OF FABRIC** stated as an age — "the old wall", "new-cut timber", "weathered", "raised in living memory" on a four-hundred-year town | `OverviewTab.jsx:251`, `:259` print `{hist.age} years old` and a `historicalCharacter` line. **Age-flavour is now FREE where it does not contradict the printed age** — "older than the road", "older than the arrangement that pays for it" | ALL |
| **F2-08** | **A TREND** — "worse than last season", "it has grown", "larger each time", a legitimacy or piety charted over time | R-γ: a trend asserts a past STATE the engine does not hold and will later compute differently. `faithPanelModel.js:79` (the arc is prospective); `stressorsStateProse.js:329-331` | ALL |
| **F2-09** | **A DEPENDENCY ON A FIELD THE POOL KEY CANNOT SEE** — an allusion to the town's past on a key that reads no history field | `historyPreservation.js:1-30` — "Reroll history replaces `settlement.history` wholesale"; `operationRegistry.js:311`. **No state-prose pool key reads a history field**, so a historical allusion desyncs on a button press, not only on a tick | ALL |

**The conversion that makes the prose better, not merely legal.** Turn the history you wanted into a STANDING CONDITION. Not *the mill burned three winters back* but *the mill's upper floor is not used and nobody will say plainly why.* Not *forty on the roll* but *the muster ground is bigger than the muster.* Not *built in the old lord's time* but *the gate is older work than the wall it hangs in.* A date closes a question; a standing condition opens one.

