# FLOOR 4 — THE ENGINE'S OWN POSITIVE MODEL `[F4]`

| id | the claim that would be false | the field / file:line | binds |
|---|---|---|---|
| **F4-01** | **A ROTTING, WEATHERING OR ERODING WALL.** ⛔ **RE-CUT WORDING:** *no material DECAY CLOCK exists (no rot, no weathering, no erosion; "timber rots" and "stone endures" are refused even where common sense agrees)* — **and never "walls never decay"**, because `calamityKernel.js:96-151`, `:251`, `:259-275` DEMOTES built fabric along `UPGRADE_CHAIN_PAIRS` (`City walls and gates` → `Town walls` → `Palisade or earthworks`), stamps `status:'ruined'`, and `razingExecution.js` / `settlementLifecycleFirstClass.js` raze it. **So: no decay clock, AND no face asserts the PERMANENCE of any institution row.** The one clock over built fabric is the calamity-scar half-life, keyed on the calamity kind (`urbanFabricKernel.js:644-647`) | ALL |
| **F4-02** | **TWO PURSES SPLIT AT BIRTH** — the wall kept and the muster not; the wall paid for itself; the watch flush while the muster starves | `defenseGenerator.js:182`, `:189-192` — ONE multiplier `milUpkeepMult = min(1, 0.6 + econOutput/50 × 0.4)` over "garrison wages, wall maintenance" TOGETHER, on the funded portion above the unpaid community baseline. The generator's asymmetry is in the CONSEQUENCE, not the pay: a built wall keeps standing (`:184-187`) | DEF ALL |
| **F4-03** | **SPLITTING THE DIRECTION OF THE FOUR GATES** — patrols provisioned while the gaol starves; the watch paid and the muster not | all four are `min(1, floor + econOutput/50 × (1−floor))` on ONE input: military 0.6 (`:189`), monster 0.7 (`:223`), internal/order 0.65 (`:251`), disaster 0.55 (`:614`). **They differ in degree only, never in direction.** Per-institution variation is licensed ONLY on the world-run's typed impairments (`institutionStatusModel.js:118`: supply_shortage · corruption_exposed · damage · siege_occupation — none of them "unpaid") | DEF ALL |
| **F4-04** | **A TOTAL COLLAPSE OF PAY** — "nothing has been paid in a year", "there is no watch left to pay", an emptied town | every gate has a FLOOR and `communityMilBase` is exempt entirely (`defenseGenerator.js:186-192`). The licensed extreme is short, late, thin — never none. **Men drifting off slowly IS the model's own word** (`:186-187`, "unpaid soldiers desert slowly"); a headcount is F2-01 | DEF |
| **F4-05** | `plagued` read as DISEASE | `monsterThreat.js:28`; `SummaryTab.jsx:28`, `:37` print "plagued by MONSTER activity"; disease is the separate `plague_onset` stress (`stressTypes.js:84-92`). ⚠ and the same page can print "the constant monster threat keeps the guard exceptionally well-drilled and alert" (`safetyProfile.js:276`) — a cowed, sickened `plagued` town contradicts that branch | ALL |
| **F4-06** | the readiness band explained by the works | `defenseGenerator.js:510` — `readiness = avgScore + tierBonus − threatPenalty`; the band moves while every wall, gate and roster row is unchanged; `:491` gives +12 for being cheap to defend | DEF |
| **F4-07** | the river or the coast doing nothing for the town's defence | `defenseGenerator.js:129-135` — riverside and coastal carry a small POSITIVE multiplier | DEF |
| **F4-08** | magic written into a world where magic does not work; or a magical CRITICAL read as the town's own failing | `magicWorksAt.js:49-53`; `defenseGenerator.js:295-307`, `:502-505` (`scores.magical` reads a WORLD) | DEF |
| **F4-09** | a blockade closing a harbour, a road or supply outright | `blockadeTransport.js:19-28` — the engine impairs rows matching `/airship/i` ONLY, and "impaired, never inoperable"; the only bypasses are teleport and airship (`foodStockpile.js:313-316`) | WF DEF |
| **F4-10** | crises COMPOUNDING — "each makes the others harder to end" | `stressGenerator.js:339-346` (independent rolls); `stressorDynamics.js:458-460` ("everything not listed keeps today's behavior (no interaction)") outside the listed synergies | STR |
| **F4-11** | a house falling derelict, failing or going quiet in the economy | `economicState.js:692-720` — NO condition, age or wear is modelled anywhere this desk reads; only the calamity ruin filter removes a house. The economy analogue of F4-01 | ECO |
| **F4-12** | the sink growing or shrinking off the devotion trend; two creeds in different niches not competing; temper and alignment as two independent choices | `religiousContest.js:932` and `religionState.js:386-395` (the sink's kinetics are `secularPull` and `crisisDisorder`); `religionState.js:68-71`, `:283-285` (cross-niche contest and capacity-full eviction ARE modelled); `deityAxes.js:148-153` (the temper is DERIVED from the alignment axes) | WF |
| **F4-13** | **AUDIENCE: a PLAYER face naming a fact the engine flags COVERT** | `impairments[].covert` (`corruption.js:670-681`) and the unexposed-stooge route (`:648-651`, `:683-689` — the DM line names the OFFICE, never the officer); `blocs[].covert` (`settlementPolitics.js:423-436`); `mobilization` covert (`mobilization.js:128`, `:147`); the brokerage patron, covert iff `house.legality === 'illegal'`, whose PLAYER PROJECTION writes `patronName: 'unknown'` (`brokeragePatronage.js:296`, `:326`); the attacker's identity on `unattributed` (F1-70). **The positive move nobody used: the player face may say the town DOES NOT KNOW, and the not-knowing is the hook** | POW STR WF ECO |
| **F4-14** | a corruption the roster PUBLISHES called hidden | `npcGenerator.js:1524`, `:1532` — `'Corrupt Official'` is a mandated, openly-rostered public role string | POW DEF |
| **F4-15** | the capture rungs read at the wrong threshold | three thresholds, and they are different facts: birth `adversarial` (`holderTable.js:129-143`), world `corrupted`/`capture` (`:659-661`), and `rulingStructure.js:762-767` (`adversarial` asserts enforcement is WINNING) | POW DEF |
| **F4-16** | a resource worked out for good, or a renewable exhausted | `resourceSemantics.js` recovery modes — renewable never exhausts | ECO |
| **F4-17** | a smelting, milling or processing step with no house for it | `economicState.js:692-720`; the roster | ECO |
| **F4-18** | naming any of the six force buckets on the `NO organized force at all` key | `defenseStateProse.js:1273` — the key consults SIX buckets, so the pool's own key licenses the denial and denies the body | DEF |
| **F4-19** | the pay gate not reaching the watch | `defenseGenerator.js:177-178`, `:189-191` (`hasAnyDefense` counts `hasWatch`); `fieldSynonyms.js:51` calls the gate "the town's pay for its watch"; `:244-253` the order purse pays "watch wages, court and gaol funding". **The watch arms BOTH purses — rule 5's old bar is struck** | DEF |

