## THE ONE SENTENCE

**Do not seat a body, a building, a record-keeper, a force or a faith-house the town's roster does not hold; do not read an engine label at its English sense where the engine prints its own sense beside the prose; do not speak a magnitude or a tense the record does not hand you; and do not deny what the engine positively models.** Everything else is yours.
